WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.341
My name is William Crabtree.

2
00:00:08.102 --> 00:00:11.185
I was a young boy in England in the year 1800.

3
00:00:11.805 --> 00:00:16.309
In those days some people became very rich by putting machines into factories.

4
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.952
This change was called the Industrial Revolution.

5
00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:24.476
Before machines were invented, all the work had to be done by hand.

6
00:00:25.377 --> 00:00:28.540
But with machines, things could be done much more quickly.

7
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.302
This was wonderful for the factory owners, but it was awful for the workers.

8
00:00:35.342 --> 00:00:38.464
The machines were dangerous and created a lot of dirt.

9
00:00:39.184 --> 00:00:42.525
Even worse, the factory owners treated the workers very badly.

10
00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:46.607
The owners only cared about their money and their machines.

11
00:00:48.528 --> 00:00:53.530
In those days a man was paid about ten shillings a day, which is less than one dollar.

12
00:00:54.191 --> 00:00:59.945
However, children were paid only two shillings a day, so the owners liked to hire poor children to

13
00:00:59.985 --> 00:01:01.026
work in their factories.

14
00:01:01.966 --> 00:01:02.926
It was terrible work.

15
00:01:04.007 --> 00:01:07.308
I began working in a textile factory when I was eight years old.

16
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.451
A textile factory is a factory that makes cloth.

17
00:01:14.111 --> 00:01:17.073
My family was so poor that I could not go to school.

18
00:01:18.213 --> 00:01:20.374
I had to earn money so that we could live.

19
00:01:21.354 --> 00:01:24.596
I worked every day from six in the morning to ten at night.

20
00:01:25.232 --> 00:01:29.033
Even on Sundays I had to go to the factory to clean all the machines.

21
00:01:29.853 --> 00:01:31.214
It was very hard labor.

22
00:01:33.354 --> 00:01:36.975
I was so tired at night that I sometimes slept as I walked home.

23
00:01:37.956 --> 00:01:41.697
When people saw me walking home, they would tell me to quit my job.

24
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:46.718
But I couldn't because my father's wages were not enough to feed our family.

25
00:01:47.538 --> 00:01:52.580
When I got home at night, I was always hungry, but usually I was too tired to eat

26
00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:53.200
my dinner.

27
00:01:54.048 --> 00:01:55.669
I would just fall down and sleep.

28
00:01:59.069 --> 00:02:01.610
Sometimes in the morning, I could not wake up.

29
00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:05.831
So my father would carry me to the factory while I was still sleeping.

30
00:02:06.512 --> 00:02:07.732
But I couldn't be late.

31
00:02:08.552 --> 00:02:11.093
If I were late for work, I would be in big trouble.

32
00:02:11.973 --> 00:02:16.695
My friend David was often late for work, so the owner often beat him with a strap.

33
00:02:20.716 --> 00:02:22.492
I was a piecer.

34
00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:27.434
All day I had to lean over the spinning machine, which was the machine that made the cloth.

35
00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:31.315
Piecers had to tie pieces of thread together when they broke.

36
00:02:32.115 --> 00:02:35.296
If the thread was broken, the machine could not make the cloth.

37
00:02:36.176 --> 00:02:39.177
So it was very important for us to do our job correctly.

38
00:02:41.557 --> 00:02:44.318
We were always running, and we could never sit down.

39
00:02:45.379 --> 00:02:47.679
It was very difficult to keep up with the work.

40
00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.160
We also had to work quickly.

41
00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:52.618
The owner also beat slow children.

42
00:02:53.739 --> 00:02:55.541
We were all very afraid of him.

43
00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.382
He was a bad man.

44
00:03:00.786 --> 00:03:02.267
A piecer's work was dangerous.

45
00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:04.929
We had to put our hands into the machine.

46
00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:09.734
If a piecer fell or was too slow, very bad things could happen.

47
00:03:10.515 --> 00:03:13.918
Many of my friends got badly hurt, and some even died.

48
00:03:14.558 --> 00:03:15.960
We had to be very careful.

49
00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.986
The worst part of working at the factory was the food.

50
00:03:21.626 --> 00:03:27.250
We were given only a little bit of soup and some bad-tasting bread for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

51
00:03:28.271 --> 00:03:29.992
And we were not allowed to stop working.

52
00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:33.254
We had to eat our meals standing at the machines.

53
00:03:36.096 --> 00:03:41.220
Since the machines were very dirty, my food was often covered in dirt, so I had to eat

54
00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:41.980
dirty food.

55
00:03:42.781 --> 00:03:43.882
This made me very sick.

56
00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:47.064
One time a boy complained about the food.

57
00:03:47.756 --> 00:03:49.457
The owner got very angry with him.

58
00:03:50.278 --> 00:03:52.539
After that, no one ever complained again.

59
00:03:55.061 --> 00:03:59.784
Around 1833 some good men in the government tried to help the children.

60
00:04:00.465 --> 00:04:05.368
A new law made it illegal in England for a child under ten to work in a textile

61
00:04:05.408 --> 00:04:10.612
factory, and children under twelve could work no more than eight or ten hours a day.

62
00:04:11.533 --> 00:04:16.176
Also, on Sundays, the factory owners had to teach the children to read and write.

63
00:04:18.944 --> 00:04:24.526
As time passed, new laws were passed to improve the lives of children even more.

64
00:04:24.606 --> 00:04:29.748
In 1867 the laws on child labor were extended to many more industries.

65
00:04:30.589 --> 00:04:37.152
It became illegal in England to hire children to work in mines, at shipyards, and many dangerous factories,

66
00:04:37.612 --> 00:04:40.453
such as match factories and nail factories.

67
00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:46.135
Today almost every country in the world has child labor laws to protect children.

68
00:04:46.855 --> 00:04:53.571
In 1990 the United Nations agreed on the Convention on the Rights of the Child, which protects children

69
00:04:53.991 --> 00:04:57.252
not just from unfair work, but from war and disease.

70
00:04:58.153 --> 00:05:02.375
It also protects the right of children to live with their parents and go to school.

71
00:05:03.516 --> 00:05:06.317
Attitudes have changed greatly since the 1880s.

72
00:05:07.137 --> 00:05:12.240
Today childhood is cherished as a time to grow and learn in health and safety.
